{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"_meta":{"fastmcp":{"tags":[]}},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Fetch OHLCV price history for `ticker`, smart-cached via the service.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"ticker":{"type":"string"},"start_date":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"end_date":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null}},"required":["ticker"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"name":"market_data_get_price_history","outputSchema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true},"title":"Market Data Get Price History"},{"_meta":{"fastmcp":{"tags":[]}},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Fetch OHLCV price history for multiple tickers.\n\nA single bad ticker's failure is captured per-ticker in `results` rather\nthan aborting the whole batch; a shared bad `start_date`/`end_date`\n(parsed once up front), or a `tickers` list exceeding `settings.\nhistory_batch_max`, fails the whole call instead, since neither can be\nattributed to any one ticker. The happy path (including one with\nper-ticker failures) always carries a top-level `\"status\": \"success\"` so\ncallers can branch on it uniformly before looking at `results`.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"tickers":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"start_date":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null},"end_date":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}],"default":null}},"required":["tickers"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"name":"market_data_get_price_history_batch","outputSchema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true},"title":"Market Data Get Price History Batch"},{"_meta":{"fastmcp":{"tags":[]}},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Fetch a single quote (TTL-cached by the service).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"ticker":{"type":"string"}},"required":["ticker"],"type":"object","additionalProperties":false},"name":"market_data_get_quote","outputSchema":{"type":